## Phase 2 — tab strip advanced interactions (auditA #8b)
- Middle-click close: Down(Middle) on the strip closes the tab on
  the PRESS (session-tabs.tsx:1657-1664 — no select, no drag arm);
  the home pseudo-tab's middle click follows the ✕ fallback.
- Right-click context menu: Down(Right) on a tab opens
  DialogKind::TabMenu { session_id, x, y } — a new Family::Menu
  dialog rendered AT the press (left clamped into the terminal, top
  one row under; NO backdrop dim — v2's capture layer is
  invisible), rows-only (no title/filter/footer chrome). Contents
  per v2 TabContextMenu (session-tabs.tsx:391-417): tab-scoped =
  New session / Rename / Copy session ID / Close; strip-scoped
  (the `+`, the home pseudo-tab, or empty strip cells) = the
  recently-closed list (≤ 10) with reopen actions, or the muted
  empty row. Submits: new→Home, rename→SessionRename dialog, copy→
  OSC-52 + toast, close→close_tab, reopen:{id}→reopen_tab.
  A right-press inside an open menu closes it (the scrollbox's own
  onMouseDown, :470). Keyboard: the dialog layer's up/down/enter/
  escape ride unchanged.
- Drag reorder: Down(Left) on a tab arms the drag (App::strip_drag);
  Drag(Left) maps the column to the visible slot (slotAt's overflow
  + widths walk) and previews locally (Store::drag_preview →
  strip_tabs_ordered applies moveSessionTab); Up(Left) persists ONE
  move and selects the source (release, :1505-1514) — the strip
  renders the preview order via paint_solid_bar_held.
- Close-hold: the ✕ release arms Store::CloseHold { items, ids,
  widths, closed, target, x, expires } (holdCloseCell, :1481-1503)
  and the layout FREEZES through held_session_tab_layout (the
  session-tabs.tsx:240-278 port — the target tab's width stretches
  so its ✕ sits at the pointer's column): strip_hit_with_layout +
  StripInputs.held consume it for hit-testing and painting. Lazy
  5 s expiry on the store clock; a left press on a tab releases it.
- The vertical rail variant: not ported — the rail layout (width ≤
  SESSION_TABS_COMPACT_BREAKPOINT sidebar-tabs mode) is outside the
  port's covered layouts (auditA §2.2); registered.
- Registered approximation: the menu's row chrome reuses the select
  option rows (title at the 4-wide marker column), so the box is
  +6 over v2's scrollbox width math.
- Tests: mouse_strip_middle_click_closes_on_down,
  mouse_strip_right_click_menu_actions (open/at-press geometry, all
  four actions, reopen row), mouse_strip_drag_reorders_on_release
  (preview + persist + plain-click no-reorder),
  mouse_strip_close_hold_freezes_the_layout_for_rapid_closes
  (second ✕ at the same column + expiry). oc-tui lib: 680/680.

## Phase 3 — tool-row affordances (auditA #9)
- tool_cell_hit now follows v2's per-family arm table
  (session/index.tsx): execute + background shells → the detail
  dialog on click AND error-click (:3207-3218, unchanged from
  SURF-1); the Subagent/Task row → NavigateToSession via metadata
  sessionID/sessionId (:3083-3112); write/edit/patch BlockTool
  cards NEVER arm (no onClick, :2989-3016); read/glob/grep/
  webfetch/websearch arm only while FAILED (the InlineTool error
  reveal, :2656-2668); the generic tool arms while expandable
  (input present) or failed (:2548). Registered approximation: the
  shell card arms always (v2 gates on shellID||overflow — the
  port's shell block always carries collapsible output); the
  execute CALL rows toggle through the part-level disclosure (v2
  arms each ExecuteCallView; the port's expanded model is
  per-part).
- The failed InlineTool families render the error reveal
  (tool_detail.rs error_reveal): expanded → assistant_error_row
  stacked under the head, for read/glob/grep/webfetch/websearch.
- Clickable links (ui/link.tsx:27): StyledSpan + Atom carry the
  markdown chunk `link` URLs end-to-end (chunk_span →
  flatten_spans → wrap_atoms → styled_runs → the placed runs); the
  transcript hit walk arms one tight rect per link LABEL run
  (part: text/reasoning rows) → TranscriptHitAction::OpenLink →
  Store::open_url (xdg-open detached; a test sink observes).
  hyperlinks_supported stays false (v2 headless parity — enabling
  it shifts the pipeline's conceal/highlight resolution; the two
  debug-dump syntax goldens re-pinned for the new span field).
  Registered limitation: bare URLs (no markdown label) need the
  OSC-8 profile — only labeled [label](url) links arm.
- session.toggle.exploration_grouping now actually ungroups:
  part_path consults the flag (v2 index.tsx:233/240), threaded
  through reduce_rows_with_rules.
- The strip close-hold releases when the pointer leaves the strip
  (the onMouseOut bounds check) — the pty_interactions close test
  routes off-strip before the ` + ` click (v2-faithful freeze
  would otherwise pin the plus past the pointer).
- Tests: subagent_row_navigates_to_the_child_session,
  tool_row_arms_follow_the_v2_table (failed read arms + reveals,
  settled read/write never arm, generic expandable),
  markdown_link_click_opens_the_url (sink-recorded openUrl).
  Full: oc-tui + oc-tui-core 845/845.

## Phase 4 — toast action + home footer chips (auditA #10)
- ToastOptions gained action_command (v2's action.run → its dot
  command) + with_action(); set_mcp_servers now produces v2's
  toast-once alerts (app.tsx:522-545): failed/needs_auth
  transitions, per-server dedup, action "Open MCP servers" →
  mcp.list. The F11 gate narrowed to a `modal` flag (the
  Session-failed/send-failure surfaces keep swallowing keys; every
  other toast — v2's rule — stays transparent; the MCP error toast
  no longer blocks typing).
- Pointer surface (ui/toast.tsx:57-59): hover inside the panel
  pauses the countdown (Moved), leaving resumes; a release inside
  ACTIVATES — toast_activate() dismisses + dispatches the action
  command through the palette dispatcher. The rect mirrors
  toast_geometry + the panel rows (panel_rows_public).
- Keyboard: `toast.activate` (PORT ADDITION, ctrl+alt+t, palette
  Prompt — registered in the coverage test's additions list)
  reaches the same activate path from the input layer.
- Home footer chips: HomeView.plugins_failed (the boot resolution's
  failures → store signal) renders v2's `⊙ N plugin(s) failed`
  chip (+ `/plugins` hint at ≥80) after the MCP cell; plan_home
  computes both cells' hit extents → FooterChipHits (store
  registry, cleared on navigate/footer-hide). Up(Left) on home
  dispatches mcp.list / plugins.list.
- Tests: toast_pointer_surface_pauses_and_activates (hover pause +
  inside release → the action opened the MCP dialog),
  toast_activate_chord_fires_the_action, mcp_failure_transitions_
  toast_once (title/action/non-modal + the same-status dedup),
  home_footer_chips_are_clickable (both cells → their dialogs).
  Full suite: 849/849.
